    content: "Rajiv Malhotra runs a mid-size export business in Mumbai. In early 2026, after watching MicroStrategy and other companies add Bitcoin to their treasury, he convinced his board to allocate 5% of their cash reserves to Bitcoin. The amount: approximately Rs.17 crore, or about 25 BTC.\n\nRajiv first tried to buy through a regular exchange. He placed a market order for 5 BTC as a test. The price slipped 0.8% by the time the order filled because his buy was larger than the available liquidity at the listed price. On Rs.3.5 crore, that slippage cost him about Rs.2,80,000.\n\nAt that rate, buying the full 25 BTC would have cost lakhs extra in slippage alone. Plus the transaction would have been visible on the public order book, potentially moving the market further against him.\n\nA friend in the crypto space suggested IndiaBitcoin's OTC desk. The OTC (over the counter) desk handles large trades privately, outside the public order book. Minimum order: 25 BTC. Custom price matching against major exchanges. Dedicated account manager.\n\nRajiv spoke to the OTC team on a Wednesday. By Friday, they had agreed on a price that was within 0.1% of the market rate. The trade was executed in a single block, with no market impact. The total savings compared to buying on the open market was estimated at Rs.8-10 lakh.\n\nThe OTC desk also handled compliance documentation that Rajiv's company needed for their auditors. Everything was clean, traceable, and above board.\n\nRajiv has since recommended the OTC desk to three other business owners. For institutional-size purchases, the OTC desk is not a luxury. It is a necessity. The math simply does not work any other way.\n\nAs of April 2026, the 25 BTC sits on IndiaBitcoin's institutional custody, earning nothing but appreciating steadily. Rajiv calls it the best board decision of the year.",
