    title: "My Online Store Now Accepts Bitcoin via Lightning. Sales Went Up 18%.",
    excerpt: "Priya runs a handicraft store in Jaipur. Adding Lightning Network payments brought her international customers she never had before.",
    content: "Priya Rathore runs a small online store selling Rajasthani handicrafts from Jaipur. Block-printed fabrics, blue pottery, and handmade jewelry. Her customers were mostly domestic, paying via UPI or card.\n\nShe always wanted to sell internationally. The craftsmanship was world-class, and there was clear demand from tourists who visited Jaipur. But international payment processing was a nightmare. Credit card processors charged 3.5% plus currency conversion. PayPal held funds for 21 days for new sellers. And many potential customers from South America and Southeast Asia did not have international credit cards at all.\n\nA fellow artisan at a trade fair mentioned that she had started accepting Bitcoin payments. Priya was confused. Bitcoin was volatile. She did not want to receive payment in something that could lose 10% overnight.\n\nThe artisan explained IndiaBitcoin's Auto Sell feature. You get a Bitcoin address. When a customer pays, the Bitcoin is instantly converted to INR and deposited in your bank account. You never actually hold Bitcoin. The fee is zero percent.\n\nPriya set it up in 15 minutes. She added a Lightning payment option to her Shopify store. Within the first week, she got three orders from Brazil, two from Thailand, and one from Nigeria. None of these customers had ever been able to pay her before.\n\nThe Lightning payments settled in seconds. Priya saw the INR in her bank account the same day. No 21-day holds. No 3.5% processing fees. No currency conversion headaches.\n\nIn the first three months, Bitcoin payments accounted for 18% of her revenue. Not because her existing customers switched, but because a whole new market of international buyers could now reach her.\n\nPriya did not become a Bitcoin investor. She became a Bitcoin merchant. And her business has never been more global.\n\nShe now teaches other Jaipur artisans how to set up Lightning payments. She calls it the new Silk Road, except this one is completely legal.",
